# Netlify reads this file automatically and applies these headers to every
# response. If you host elsewhere (GitHub Pages, Vercel, Cloudflare Pages),
# see README.md for the equivalent for that platform — GitHub Pages in
# particular cannot set custom headers at all, which is the main reason
# Netlify or Cloudflare Pages is recommended over it for this site.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-XSS-Protection: 0
